 ## Overview
-Partially Learned Gradient Descent is an iterative reconstruction method that unrolls a fixed number of optimization steps into a neural network, combining a fixed physics-based gradient step with a learnable neural network update [S1, unofficial]. It initializes the reconstruction with a filtered backprojection (FBP) estimate and, in its base form, does not use a regularization term in the network input [S1, unofficial]. Unlike standard Gradient Descent which uses a fixed step size, this method learns the update rule via a convolutional network while retaining the physical forward model and gradient structure, making it more interpretable and robust to distribution shifts than fully learned end-to-end CNNs [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Gradient Descent Solver](3280-gradient-descent-solver.md).
+Partially Learned Gradient Descent is an iterative reconstruction method that unrolls a fixed number of optimization steps into a neural network, combining a fixed physics-based gradient step with a learnable convolutional network update [S1, unofficial]. It initializes the reconstruction with a filtered backprojection (FBP) estimate and, in its base form, does not use a regularization term in the network input [S1, unofficial]. Unlike standard Gradient Descent which uses a fixed step size, this method learns the update rule via convolutional layers while retaining the physical forward model and gradient structure, making it more interpretable and robust to distribution shifts than fully learned end-to-end CNNs [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Gradient Descent Solver](3280-gradient-descent-solver.md) [G].
 
